00:13:25.221 --> 00:13:27.028
Ladies and gentlemen, Mountain Dew.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.450
I will go to my grave knowing
that flavor all too well.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.120
I don't know why they just
don't get regular fruit punch.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.900
They have the Gatorade, the
G2 Gatorade fruit punch.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:37.000
Pink lemonade.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.560
So, I heard that pink lemonade

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.418
is just lemonade that's dyed pink.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:45.620
Just tastes like lemonade.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.253
What's in pink lemonade
that makes it pink?

00:13:47.253 --> 00:13:49.320
It was originally, like,
it was invented by,

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.010
I think, a traveling circus.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.690
And they just did it kind
of to get people to buy it.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.530
Like, it was a novelty.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.150
It was pink instead of
regular lemonade color.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.240
But I'm assuming now they do something,

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.730
they must do something to pink
lemonade to make it taste ...

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.953
That's lemonade.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:08.110
What makes pink lemonade
different from lemonade?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.270
I want to know.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.680
Our Taco Bell also has
coffee and iced coffee.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.320
And although I would never drink
this, unsweetened iced tea.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.470
Taco Bell's got breakfast in
the US, and I have to say,

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:19.080
I think that their
breakfast menu is fantastic.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.460
If it looks a little scarce,

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.000
it is because I don't think
they gave me everything.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.050
And I'm confused on what
some of these things are,

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.540
because everything's kind of wrapped.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:28.697
They used to have, like,

00:14:28.697 --> 00:14:30.640
didn't they used to have,
like, a waffle taco?

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.490
Maybe I'm just imagining that.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.690
They got a cheesy
toasted breakfast burrito

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.170
and a cheesy toasted
breakfast burrito with potato.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.370
And, of course, they have a

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:43.070
hash brown toasted breakfast burrito,

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.294
which I think is this.

00:14:44.294 --> 00:14:47.000
Hash brown toasted breakfast
burrito with steak,

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.660
which is right here.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:52.140
And, of course, the grande
toasted breakfast burrito,

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.250
which is right here.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.710
And, of course, they have

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.150
the grande toasted breakfast
burrito with steak.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:00.762
And then they have a breakfast Crunchwrap.

00:15:00.762 --> 00:15:03.953
Yo, this one has eggs

00:15:03.953 --> 00:15:06.211
and potato in it.

00:15:06.211 --> 00:15:07.580
It looks ridiculous.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.010
But for real, when these are hot,

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.420
at, like, 9:30 in the
morning, you can't beat this.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:13.420
As a matter of fact ...

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.426
This is so good.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:24.380
Even sitting out for a couple
hours, it's still awesome.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.350
Taco Bell's breakfast is great.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:27.210
They're no McGriddles,

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.130
but if a McDonald's isn't available,

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:30.610
I'll go right to Taco Bell breakfast.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.890
You can also get ...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.800
Hash brown. Can you see him there?

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.060
Breakfast salsas. These are really good.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:37.893
Orange juice.

00:15:37.893 --> 00:15:40.313
The homies over at
Tropicana holding it down.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:44.430
Let's talk about nutrition.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:47.021
In Japan, a beef crunchy taco

00:15:47.021 --> 00:15:50.900
is 164.4 calories.

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:54.290
It has 87.2 grams of protein,

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.774
5.5 grams of fat,

00:15:56.774 --> 00:15:59.657
14.7 grams of carbs,

00:15:59.657 --> 00:16:03.530
and 293 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.530
In the US, our standard beef crunchy taco

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.305
is 170 calories,

00:16:07.305 --> 00:16:10.100
8 grams of protein, 9 grams of fat,

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.920
13 grams of carbs, and
310 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.650
So we lead in calories, fat, and sodium,

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:18.720
where Japan has more protein and carbs.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.290
The next one is the chicken quesadilla.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.640
Ours has 492.51 calories.

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:28.900
This one has 510 calories.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:29.789
One thing to note:

00:16:29.789 --> 00:16:32.157
that in both countries,
one of these quesadillas

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:35.340
hovers around half of your daily sodium.

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:38.030
Sodium at Taco Bell
appears to be such an issue

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.940
that in the US menu online,
certain combos and items,

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:44.460
like this one right here, are
labeled with sodium warnings.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.050
In Japan, a Crunchwrap Supreme

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:51.290
has 1,290 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:55.380
That's 56% of your daily allowance.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:59.190
Our Crunchwrap Supreme
is 52% your daily sodium.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.770
That's more than half, right?

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:03.810
Man, so both countries,
way too much sodium.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:07.770
Are you looking for the most
calories in one menu item?

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:11.150
In Japan, it's our loaded fries.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.540
One order is 718 calories.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.230
It has a third of your daily calories,

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:19.171
almost half of your daily fat,

00:17:19.171 --> 00:17:22.446
and 66% of your daily sodium.

00:17:22.446 --> 00:17:23.720
In the US, the biggest thing

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.080
you should look out for are the nachos.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.277
The very popular Nachos BellGrande,

00:17:27.277 --> 00:17:28.110
I love you guys,

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.518
is 740 calories,

00:17:30.518 --> 00:17:32.801
1,050 milligrams of sodium.

00:17:32.801 --> 00:17:37.360
OK. Now, the Cinnabon Delights
do have more calories, 930.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.850
But technically that's a 12-pack,

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.580
which is supposed to be for four people.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.670
I'm certain, if you're like me,

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.330
you're getting 12 and
you're not sharing them.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.670
Some do, most don't, but obviously

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:48.620
the Nachos BellGrande is for one person.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.540
But the most calories lie in an item

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.500
that's on Taco Bell's cantina menu,

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.788
which is only available

00:17:53.788 --> 00:17:55.263
at certain locations here in the US.

00:17:55.263 --> 00:17:58.210
There, you can get something
called the grande beef nachos,

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:02.470
which has 1,120 calories,

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.220
which is more than half
of your daily allowance,

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.290
and 68% of your daily sodium.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.531
[sighs]

00:18:08.531 --> 00:18:10.956
Now, it's just not the food at Taco Bell.

00:18:10.956 --> 00:18:13.180
You also have to watch out for the drinks.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:14.520
Here it is, everyone.

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:18.990
30 fluid ounces of
Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.680
A beverage that answers the question,

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.640
"What if we combined Mountain Dew's bold,

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:25.650
refreshing tropical
flavor with crystal meth?"

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:29.320
This totally logical 30 fluid
ounces of nightmare fuel

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:32.070
is 420 calories, very cool,

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:34.550
and 110 grams of sugar.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.470
I don't know. Sorry.

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:37.170
This stuff is making me delirious.

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:44.020
In the US, there are a few
ingredients at our Taco Bell

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.190
you should look out for.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:48.040
Both are in the beverages
on Taco Bell's cantina menu.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:51.023
First is brominated vegetable oil,

00:18:51.023 --> 00:18:53.148
aka BVO,

00:18:53.148 --> 00:18:54.510
which is banned in Japan.

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:57.630
BVO is an emulsifier found
in citrus-flavored sodas

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.970
and is specifically used with citrus oils,

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:01.230
and it's considered a health risk

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:02.610
when ingested in large amounts.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:04.380
It was brought to public attention

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.200
when it was discovered
in popular beverages

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.870
like Mountain Dew and Powerade,
but due to public pressure,

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.050
it was removed from
Coke and Pepsi products

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.053
in 2014, which is good.

00:19:13.053 --> 00:19:15.800
Now, unfortunately, you can
still find this ingredient

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.504
in three cantina menu freezes.

00:19:18.504 --> 00:19:21.350
The beach berry freeze,
the ginger mule freeze,

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:23.330
and the party punch freeze.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.630
Luckily, they weren't
in any of the freezes

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.541
you'd find in the regular
menu, only on the cantina menu.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.670
Ugh!

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:34.060
OK. When it comes to citrus-flavored soda,

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:36.300
we have CC Lemon.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.190
That's one of the most popular

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.520
citrus-flavored soda in Japan.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:42.990
CCL Lemon contains the following:

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:46.510
sugars, which is fructose-glucose syrup

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:51.460
and sugar, lemon juice,
flavoring, vitamin C,

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:56.250
acidulant, safflower dye,
calcium pantothenate,

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.180
vitamin B6, carotene pigment.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.160
That's it.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:04.950
See? It doesn't have
brominated vegetable oil.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.150
It tastes really good.

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:09.916
So that means you can make it delicious

00:20:09.916 --> 00:20:12.765
without BVO.

00:20:12.765 --> 00:20:14.420
The last one, party punch freeze,

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:18.140
also contains Yellow
No. 5, aka tartrazine,

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:20.210
which is subject to
restrictions outside of the US

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.342
in places like the EU and Japan,

00:20:22.342 --> 00:20:24.840
as it may have "adverse effect

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:27.730
on activity and attention in children."

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.130
What the hell?

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.540
You can tell this color is yellow, right?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:37.180
So why don't you use something
else that isn't harmful?

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:40.222
Just like CC Lemon.

00:20:40.222 --> 00:20:41.466
♪ CC lemon, hey ♪

00:20:41.466 --> 00:20:43.127
♪ CC lemon, hey ♪

00:20:43.127 --> 00:20:44.764
♪ CC lemon, hey ♪

00:20:44.764 --> 00:20:45.822
Oh, God.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.113
Too much Taco Bell.

